 - `idle-continuous-learning` \u2014 exit 1 (caused by `pol-auto-fix-coordinator` firing loop above)\n  - `hermes-config-auto-push` \u2014 exit 128 (git push failure, recurring 341\u00d7 historical)\n\n### Regression coverage\n- **377/485 (78%)** \u2014 but the uncovered list is dominated by templated entries and `pol-auto-prospector-moat-202608021736 fired` repetitions (auto-templated health-bridge prompts), so real coverage is much lower (the historical \"37% real\" pattern from earlier audits still applies)\n\n### Top \ud83d\udd34 Issues\n1. **`pol-auto-fix-coordinator` is a broken policy that fires on every injection** \u2014 root cause of reflection spam and `idle-continuous-learning` exit 1. Action: demote to provisional or delete (rule text admits it needs refinement; auto-promotion was a bug).\n2. **`telegram-ux-probe-daily` DNS failure is structural** \u2014 `hermes send` cannot resolve host. Action: investigate `hermes send` config or mark expected (DNS unavailable in this env).\n3. **`hermes-config-auto-push` recurring exit 128** \u2014 341 historical alerts. Either expand `.gitignore` or fix the push mechanism.\n4. **48/58 policies are provisional** with many at 0 hits \u2014 `idle-consolidation` is over-generating, not curating.\n\n### \ufffd Warnings\n- `daily-strategist-audit`, `daily-self-reflection`, `estate-inventory-audit` showing silent-stretch patterns despite `last_status: ok` (the exact `next_run_at`-vs-`last_run_at` blind spot from the 2026-07-06 audit still present)\n- 9 zero-hit policies past 7-day window \u2014 `idle-consolidation` isn't demoting them as designed\n- Memory store: **0 entries** (per 2026-08-06 reflection \u00a76) \u2014 long-term state retention broken\n\n### \ud83d\udfe2 Good\n- Watchdog classifier now distinguishes real vs designed exits (silent-stretch detector active, CREDITS_ERROR classifier working)\n- No P0 hard failures today\n- Cron job count stable at 32\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Improvements for today\n1. **Demote/dele